(If You&rsquo;re Still Alive to Pay)</h2>\n\n<div class=\"leaderboard\">\n  <strong>&#9733; TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK &#9733;</strong>\n  Sir Caprice &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +63 turfs<br>\n  Free Willy &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +43 turfs<br>\n  Donald Trump &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +15 turfs<br>\n  Flattop &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +11 turfs<br>\n  Wu-Tang &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +1 turf\n</div>\n\n<h3>The Annihilator Catches His Breath — But Only Barely</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">Sir Caprice Posts a Modest Sixty-Three Turfs, Raises an Army of Nearly Seven Thousand, and the City Exhales — Prematurely</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Our Man in the Trenches, Ignatius P. Flambeau</span>\n\n<p>This correspondent arrived at his desk on Monday morning fully prepared to compose a suicide note on behalf of Vendetta City's remaining independent operators. Last fortnight's front page — in which we documented the apocalyptic reign of <strong>Sir Caprice</strong>, \"The Annihilator,\" and his seizure of one hundred and sixty turfs in a single week — left this city's underworld shaking like a reed in a typhoon. The news this week, while considerably less catastrophic in raw numerical terms, is in certain respects <em>more</em> alarming.</p>\n\n<p>Sixty-three turfs claimed. Fifty raids executed with surgical precision. Five hundred territorial assaults launched across all fronts. And yet the figure that truly chills the blood is this: Sir Caprice has grown his private army by <strong>three hundred and eighty-seven gangsters in a single week</strong>, bringing his total garrison to a staggering <strong>7,342 souls</strong> — every last one of them presumably mean, well-armed, and loyal to a fault. Last week he conquered. This week he <em>consolidated</em>. Dear reader, consolidation at this scale is not a sign of slowing down. It is a man reloading.</p>\n\n<p>His sixty-five territorial captures this week included the headquarters of three rival bosses — <strong>starseed</strong>, <strong>avg</strong>, and the unfortunately monikered <strong>aaaaa</strong> — all of whom have since vanished from Vendetta City entirely, their empires absorbed, their names reduced to footnotes in this very column. Furthermore, two additional enemy headquarters were stormed and <em>destroyed</em> outright, the defenders beaten so thoroughly they could not even hold the flag. When a man is too dangerous to be stopped even by the HQ rules, one begins to suspect the city itself is losing the argument.</p>\n\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"192\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Sir Caprice</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+63</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Free Willy</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"273\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"439\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+43</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Donald Trump</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"261\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+15</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Flattop</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"119\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"235\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+11</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Wu-Tang</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"147\" width=\"6\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"172\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+1</text>\n</svg>\n\n\n<h3>Free Willy Emerges From the Shadows — Forty-Three Turfs and Four Scalps</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">The River District's Favourite Enigma Dismantles Sir Clemenza Twice in Four Days</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Staff Correspondent Millicent Rafferty-Howe</span>\n\n<p>While the city's attention remained fixed upon the thunderous footsteps of Sir Caprice, a quieter but no less ruthless campaign was unfolding along the waterfront. <strong>Free Willy</strong> — that slippery, whale-of-a-character who first surfaced in our pages three weeks past — has surged to claim <strong>forty-three turfs</strong> this week, executing twenty-six territorial captures and nineteen raids that stripped his rivals of cash and hardware alike.</p>\n\n<p>Most impressively, Free Willy has distinguished himself as this week's <em>premier headquarters hunter</em>, cracking four enemy HQs with the quiet confidence of a man who has done this before and enjoyed it immensely. His most theatrical performance was reserved for the unfortunate <strong>Sir Clemenza</strong> — a boss of previously respectable standing — whose headquarters was stormed not once, but <strong>twice</strong>, on July 3rd and again on July 6th. One imagines Sir Clemenza changing the locks on a Monday only to find Free Willy already sitting in his favourite chair by Thursday. Sir Clemenza, having now lost his HQ on two occasions in the span of four days and surrendered fourteen turfs to the wider chaos, has reportedly begun forwarding his correspondence to an undisclosed location.</p>\n\n<p>Free Willy also dispatched <strong>OXFI</strong> and <strong>bbcoub</strong> to the hereafter, both of whom have since gone dark entirely. The young pretender's garrison, while a comparatively modest ninety-three souls, appears to fight with the enthusiasm of a much larger force. This correspondent recommends watching this one closely.</p>\n\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"276\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">HEAVIEST LOSSES THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Tony Soprano</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-35</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Peaky Blinders</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"262\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"428\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-23</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Wcrypto</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"171\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"337\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-15</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Sir Clemenza</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"119\" width=\"160\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"326\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-14</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Bugsy</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"147\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"280\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-10</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">starseed</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"175\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"188\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-3</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">aaaaa</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"203\" width=\"11\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"177\" y=\"216\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-1</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">avg</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"231\" width=\"11\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"177\" y=\"244\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-1</text>\n</svg>\n\n\n<blockquote>\n<strong>&#9733; Special Bulletin: The Wcrypto\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"143\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">HQ RAIDS — TOP ATTACKERS</text>\n<line 